WEBVTT

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.750
We're off!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.270
Floaty, floaty!

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.670
Youko! Aya! Karen!

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.730
Morning!

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.500
Good morning.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.500
Good morning!

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.500
Good mornin'!

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.880
Ready to go?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.250
Yeah!

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.040
I'm first!

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.070
You're really fired up today, Youko!

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.650
Of course I am!

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.680
Because we're going to the beach today!

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.930
You were really looking forward to it, huh?

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.010
Alice, you brought a camera with you?

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.940
Yeah. I'm going to take
lots of pictures today.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.120
Ooh, me, me! I want to take pictures, too!

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.270
Me, too! Me, too!

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.700
Youko, you're just like a child...

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.610
I'd like to take some, too.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.240
The glittering ocean...

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.910
is nice, but I want pictures of Alice
and Karen's even more sparkly hair.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.490
Sh-Shino...

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.960
I see Shino's operating normally.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.780
Don't, Karen!

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.120
What? Don't do what?

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.120
I'm sitting next to Shino!

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.120
No, I'm sitting next to Shino!

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.190
Don't fight, you two.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.750
Shino, you should stop them.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.750
No, me!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.650
I knew this would happen.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.010
What's wrong, Aya?

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.460
I-It's not like I wanted to
sit next to you or anything!

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:48.020
What? Uh, sorry...

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.020
So... What does everyone want?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.030
Wow, you brought lots of snacks.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.780
We're supposed to eat lunch at
a beach house. Are you sure?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.670
Don't worry! I always have room!

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.700
I've brought snacks, too!

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.730
This!

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.650
That looks delicious.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.590
Hey, we're supposed to eat lunch
at a beach house. Are you sure?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.800
Don't worry! I always have space!

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.430
Alice, did you bring something, too?

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.130
Frozen tangerines and boiled eggs.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:29.900
They're an essential part
of day trips in Japan.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.310
Frozen tangerines are delicious.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.440
The boiled eggs are salted.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.440
<i>Her knowledge is as biased as ever.</i>

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:49.850
Seaside Promise

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.030
It's the ocean!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.650
I can smell the ocean.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.410
The breeze is so salty.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.630
It's pretty hot out here.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:14.910
Okay, everyone!

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.920
Let's shout together!

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.290
Aloha!

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:25.400
Shino, we're in Japan, not Hawaii.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.840
She must think it works like "yahoo."

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.100
Aloha!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:31.970
Youko?

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.450
We're at the beach, guys! The beach!

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.500
Aloha!

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.340
Aloha!

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.280
Aloha!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.110
W-Wait...

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.800
A-Aloha!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.360
It's the beach. It's really the beach...

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.010
What? The beach?

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.010
Glare

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.010
Yes. I want to go to the beach.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.100
I really want to go.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.020
B-But we have work to do...

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.870
I actually tried on a new swimsuit

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.450
and went swimming in my bathtub, but...

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.140
It's so small.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:28.280
It just made me feel sad.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.550
Let's go to the beach, Sensei!

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.210
What? Really?

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.520
Kuzehashi-sensei, let's go.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.570
No, first we should rent parasols and
deckchairs from the beach house.

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.770
Are your valuables secured?

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.630
We might need to rent a coin locker, as well.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.970
And just in case, we should
locate the lifeguard tower.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.680
Did you bring flip-flops?

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.050
If you go barefoot,
you might hurt yourself.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.670
We should put ours on immediately.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:57.930
O-Okay...

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:03.600
Yeah!

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:14.160
Alice, you look great in your swimsuit.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.240
You think so?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.200
Aya-chan made the right choice.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.090
You chose Alice's swimsuit for her?

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:25.850
Yes, and Alice picked out mine for me.

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.090
You both look great.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.500
Really? Do I look grown up?

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.540
Yeah, like a cute grown-up!

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:34.310
You're lying.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.140
You always show your
canines when you're lying.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.980
I don't lie that often!

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.950
What about me?

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.250
I think I look pretty good.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.380
You look fantastic, Karen.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.470
Yeah, you look great.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:52.740
You're supposed to say, "Nice body, girlie."

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.410
We're not dirty old men!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.080
Stare...

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.970
You have a really nice body, Youko.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.000
Really?

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:03.970
It's kind of frustrating!

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.890
Let me find what makes your
body different from mine.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.000
Hey, stop that!

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.350
Come on, just a little...

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:12.350
H-Hey, stop! You're gonna pull it off!

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:15.010
So? What's wrong with that?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.010
Ouch!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.130
N-Not even my dad has ever hit me!

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.270
Kusshi-chan hasn't been scolding you enough!

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:22.890
Darn it!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.600
Huh? Shino, you're not
putting on your swimsuit?

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.350
Didn't you know?

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:34.590
People in foreign countries used
to use old clothes as swimsuits.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:39.160
Shino's taking on Mother Nature!

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.290
You lose!

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.420
What is she trying to do?

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.890
What a beautiful view.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.800
It's so relaxing.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:00.370
Oh, right.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:05.000
Here, take this, Kuzehashi-sensei.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:06.810
Let's toast.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.400
Oh, okay.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.070
Let's have lots of fun today.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.070
Okay.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.260
Kuzehashi-sensei?

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.620
Sunscreen!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.280
I'd be setting a bad example
if I showed up at school

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.870
Rub Rub

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:26.920
with a tan after summer vacation.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:27.870
So serious!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.370
Nangoku Beach House Rest Area

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:32.370
Shaved Ice

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.650
Aya, what are you putting on yourself? Oil?

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.600
Oh, oil! So shiny!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.810
It's sunscreen!

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:49.680
What? If you don't tan,
we can't pretend to be roast pigs!

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.310
I'm not playing that game!

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:54.520
No fair. Let's tan together.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.320
No, I don't want to burn.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.610
I turn bright red when I get too much sun.
I look like a boiled octopus.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:04.050
Me, too. I turn bright red, and that's it.

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:06.330
I don't turn golden brown at all.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.830
That's generally true of pale people.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.560
Blonde people with tans seem kind of gaudy.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:14.590
What does "gaudy" mean?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.970
Someone like Youko.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:19.970
What? How am I gaudy?

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.680
People talk to Youko in the street all the time.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.500
Oh! You mean hitting on her?

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.850
An old lady just asked me for directions!

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.620
I guess she's the approachable type.

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.610
Youko-chan's really nice, after all.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:35.500
Basically, "gaudy" means a blonde Youko.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.860
That's a terrible thing to say!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.730
A blonde... Youko-chan?

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:40.360
Shino!

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:43.000
Shino, let's go swimming now.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.390
I really want to go swimming.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:50.370
Then I'll teach you how to swim in the ocean.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.240
First, when you walk into the water,

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.100
let it come up to your shoulders.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.280
Then start counting.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:05.210
One, two, three, four, five...

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.890
This is paradise.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:13.230
Stay with me, Shino!

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:18.310
I'm sorry. I actually can't swim.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.780
I was trying to show off.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.850
I-It's okay.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:24.260
Let's go to a shallower spot.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:27.220
We don't need swim rings here.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:28.540
You're ri—

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.820
Shino!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.150
My leg! My leg cramped!

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.300
A gangster of the sea!

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.540
Shino, run!

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.280
I'm sorry...

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.630
It's okay, Shino.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:44.030
I'll go get us some drinks.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.020
What should we do?

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.020
I want to build sand castles.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.710
We could collect shells.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.020
Good idea!

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.020
What do you want to do, Aya?

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:56.720
Me?

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:00.020
You're the one who wanted
to come to the beach.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.370
Let's do what you want to do today.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.530
Really? In that case...

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:06.780
Distance swimming.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.680
What's that?

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.640
It means swimming a really
long way in the ocean.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.780
Oh! You mean "long distance swimming," right?

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:16.770
Yeah, that's it.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.800
Very, very long swimming.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:20.160
Fine.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:21.650
I'm going.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:22.180
Huh?

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:24.380
Ayaya, you're going to swim long-distance?!

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:26.300
I was just kidding!
Don't push yourself too hard!

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:30.020
If I'm not back in ten minutes,
come and rescue me.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:31.310
You're assuming you'll drown?!

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.940
<i>Drowning means losing consciousness.</i>

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:38.530
<i>So would that mean... CPR?!</i>

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.140
I changed my mind!

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:42.770
You gave up fast!

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.200
Aya! Youko! Karen!

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:49.850
Alice!

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.110
Have you seen Shino?

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.010
No, I haven't seen her.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.210
Is something wrong?

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:58.200
She wandered off somewhere
while I went to get us drinks.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.710
Maybe she got lost on the beach.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.320
Shino's lost?

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.310
We are looking for a lost child.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:15.230
Broadcast Center

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:10.360
If you've seen a blonde-haired,
blue-eyed grade school girl

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.170
wearing a pink swimsuit,

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:15.230
please inform the beach house.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.450
Please announce it again!

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:20.730
She's a blonde <i>high school</i> girl who
<i>looks like</i> a grade school student!

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.240
It's been five minutes,
and she's still not back!

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.540
Shino's at it again...

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.990
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.040
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:37.200
Alice!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.570
I'm so glad you're all right, Alice.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.680
I can't breathe, Shino.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.280
Wasn't Shino the one who got lost?

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.180
In any case, I'm glad we found her.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.230
I'm not letting you go again!

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.660
I'll never let go!

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.020
I can't breathe...

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.280
Alice!

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.940
I really... can't breathe...

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.000
You win!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.440
Let go of her!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.210
I'm sorry! I'm sorry, Alice!

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.950
I was so happy, I couldn't help it!

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.360
I am okay. Do not worry.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.450
Broken Japanese?!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:17.700
Shino, no matter how happy you are,
you need to show some restraint.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.460
Okay...

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.960
Now, now. What should we do nex—

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.980
What's wrong, Youko?

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.090
Karen, too?

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:29.660
My stomach...

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:30.980
My stomach...

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.100
A stomachache?

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:35.780
It's because you both ate
too much on the train.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.310
Let's get you both to the hospital.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.130
I'm so... hungry...

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:42.900
Hungry...

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.990
Ow, that hurts! Show some
restraint with me, too!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.650
Ow! Sorry, sorry!

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.960
Shall we have lunch now?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.160
I said I'm sorry!

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:50.960
Yeah, let's.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:53.370
All right! It's lunchtime!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.290
Wait, I'm coming, too.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.580
Youko, wait a minute!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.120
Sheesh.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.760
I wonder what I should get.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.760
I'm starving!

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.210
Is something wrong?

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.430
No.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.510
I was just wondering if
they'd found that lost girl.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:18.210
Don't worry.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:20.740
The announcements stopped,

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.870
so that probably means they found her.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.020
You're right.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:27.470
Still, a blonde grade school student...

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.880
That sounds like someone we know, doesn't it?

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.180
You're right.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.360
There's so much to choose from!

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:38.830
There sure is.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.040
I don't know what to get.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.900
I've decided!

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:43.920
Me, too!

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.240
What are you getting, Alice?

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:50.400
I want something Japanese, like oden.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:53.270
I doubt they have oden here...

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.930
Oden

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:53.930
They do?!

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:57.200
Then I'll have a scone and royal milk tea.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:57.930
They don't have that!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.440
Hey, boss! One order of chilled Chinese noodles!

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:02.820
Make 'em freezing cold.

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.910
Just how cold do you want them?

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.750
Aya, have you decided what you're getting?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:12.070
I'll have what you're having.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.900
Here you go. "Ahh."

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.450
It's so cold!

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:26.660
This is so good!

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.500
What's wrong, Aya?
Aren't you going to eat yours?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.260
I will! I'm supposed to eat it, right?!

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.050
A-Aya?

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.790
There are so many options,
I don't know what to get.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.230
Same here.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:43.560
Excuse me.

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:46.410
I'll start with a draft beer.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:49.930
I'd also like a bowl of edamame,
cutlet skewers, and grilled rice balls.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:51.740
She knew exactly what she wanted!

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:53.840
You've gotta have yakisoba at the beach!

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:54.860
And shaved ice!

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:57.490
You still have room after all that?

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.260
I always have room.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.990
I always have space!

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:05.520
Hey, want to play beach volleyball
when you're done eating?

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.500
I do! I do!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.380
Oh! Beach volleyball!

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.800
This means the return of Demon Coach Karen!

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:15.880
Ayaya, you're too far back.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.430
Move up!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.960
Don't be ridiculous!

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:36.130
What should we get for Isami?

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:37.410
Well...

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.700
Hey! Look at this!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.340
Ta-da!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.700
I
♥
The
Blazing
Sun

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.440
Amazing! It's a mix of English and Japanese!

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.210
That looks great on you, Karen.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.850
Naturally.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:49.890
Hey!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:52.160
Isn't this one great, too?

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.100
Passionate

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.630
It's wonderful.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.410
You've got a good eye, Alice!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:00.170
Hey, we're leaving.

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.170
What? Already?

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:04.790
But I want to play some more!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.000
I want to enjoy the beach!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:10.410
Well, yeah, so do I, but...

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.680
If we don't get changed soon,
we'll catch a chill.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.190
Hey...

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:19.120
In that case, why don't we
go there before we leave?

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.440
Undersea Park

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.760
It's beautiful.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.090
Yeah.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:42.850
England is on the other
side of the ocean, isn't it?

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.940
Yeah, really far away.

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:49.010
Even if I get lonely while
you're back in England,

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:50.840
we'll still be connected by the ocean.

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.700
I'll take a raft to go see you.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.950
Shino...

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.180
The ocean hates you,
so you'd better come by plane!

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:02.850
Okay.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:03.930
Promise!

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:04.690
Okay.

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:11.290
Sorry I'm late.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.300
They're already asleep?!

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:16.250
Shh. You'll wake them.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:18.420
They're such little kids.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:21.670
They're tired. They played a lot today.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.810
You can sleep if you're tired, too.

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:25.570
You can lean on me.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:27.670
Wh-What are you saying?!

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:29.880
I'd never do that!

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:31.950
You don't have to refuse that strongly...

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.730
I'll never, ever do that!

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.360
Okay, okay.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:39.700
I'll never, ever, ever, ever, ever, ever...

00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:40.490
This is for the teachers, and this is...

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:41.870
Kuzehashi-sensei.

00:22:42.410 --> 00:22:44.410
This is so cute.

00:22:44.410 --> 00:22:45.910
Y-You're right...

00:22:45.910 --> 00:22:49.510
I know. Let's buy matching souvenirs
to remember today by.

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:50.140
What?

00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:50.920
Okay?

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:57.890
I sort of hate to leave here.

00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:58.690
What?

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:02.430
I don't want to go home yet.

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:05.120
In that case...

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:15.940
Adults need summer vacations, too.

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:17.980
You said it.

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:26.240
I want to run around laughing
and giggling on the beach...

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.270
What's that?

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:28.910
Let's play tag!

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:31.000
I'm it!

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:33.670
Dash

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.220
This isn't what I meant!

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:33.620
Yeah!

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:33.620
Wait up!

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:33.670
Laugh

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:33.670
Giggle

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:34.870
See you next time!

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.050
A Long Night

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:36.050
Aya!
